From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] topology: forward local change notification to AL-SAP

The expired-neighbor worker sends its normal multicast Topology Notification
on the network, but a locally generated frame is not received again by the
same IEEE1905 instance.  Its registered higher-layer entity therefore never
sees the change and cannot reconcile the controller topology.

After transmitting the standard multicast notification, deliver an equivalent
Topology Notification SDU through the normal AL-SAP data-indication primitive.
It contains the same AL MAC, Comcast query tag and end-of-message TLVs.  Its
AL-SAP endpoint metadata identifies the expired neighbor so the controller can
probe exactly that agent; the multicast frame remains standard and does not
expose any private TLV or event.  The controller must still use standard
Topology Query/Response behavior to determine reachability.

The lag-recovery notification no longer has the identity of each skipped
event, so it remains a multicast convergence signal and does not speculate in
the local metadata.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 ieee1905-core/src/cmdu_proxy.rs | 56 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 55 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ieee1905-core/src/cmdu_proxy.rs b/ieee1905-core/src/cmdu_proxy.rs
--- a/ieee1905-core/src/cmdu_proxy.rs
+++ b/ieee1905-core/src/cmdu_proxy.rs
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
